  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "The goal is to identify team members who may be experiencing burnout and learn how you can address it quickly and easily.\n\n### What's burnout?\n\nLearn the key [Factors of Burnout](Glint_Balance_Factors_of_Burnout) and what you can do to help prevent it: \n\nWant more? Read this article: [How To Tell If Your Team Is Burnt Out And What To Do About It](http://www.forbes.com/sites/dailymuse/2013/06/04/how-to-tell-if-your-team-is-burnt-out-and-what-to-do-about-it)\n\n### Schedule 1:1 meetings\n\nWhenever you notice signs of burnout with a team member, put a meeting on your calendars and use these [Meeting Tips](Glint_Balance_Meeting_Tips_for_Addressing_Burnout) to prepare for your discussion.\n\nAs a follow up, check in with team members who may be feeling burnt out, and continue to monitor their hours and behavior. \n\n \n\n### Reflect \n\nTake a few minutes to think how everything went:\n\n* What did you learn from looking out for burnout on your team?\n\n* Was addressing it easier or harder than you expected?\n\n* Were you able to help any team members reduce burnout? \n\n* What would you do differently next time, if anything?\n\n* Have you noticed any differences in your or the team's behavior since you've made changes?\n\n* How might you continue to do better?",
